card.statement:
A finitely generated $U$-module $M$ is called a Gelfand-Tsetlin module (with respect to $\Ga_q$) if

\begin{equation}
M=\bigoplus_{\sm\in\Sp\Ga_q}M(\sm),
\end{equation}

where $M(\sm)=\{v\in M| \sm^{k}v=0 \text{ for some }k\geq 0\}$. Equivalently,

\begin{equation}
M=\bigoplus_{\chi\in\Gamma_q^{*}}M(\chi)
\end{equation}

where $M(\chi)=\{v\in M: \forall g\in\Gamma_q\text{, }\exists k\in\mathbb{Z}_{>0} \text{ such that } (g-\chi(g))^{k}v=0 \}$.

The Gelfand-Tsetlin support of $M$ is the set $\Supp_{GT}(M):=\{\chi\in\Ga_q^{*}:M(\chi)\neq 0\}$.
